@HostAddress = http://localhost:8080
@Token = Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@savedRefreshToken = {{userLogin.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

# Credentials come from your local .env file (never hard-code them here).
# Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension, which reads .env via $dotenv.

### === HEALTH ===

### Health check (expect 200 Healthy; 503 Unhealthy if the database is down)
GET {{HostAddress}}/health


### === AUTH ===

### Login as admin (run this first; the other requests reuse its token)
# @name login
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_SEED_USERNAME}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD}}"
}

### Register a user (expect 201/200; running it twice expect 409)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}

### Register the same name in a different case (expect 409, usernames are case-insensitive)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "TESTUSER",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}

### Update a user's role (admin only)
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/user
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 2,
  "role": "admin"
}


### === CATEGORIES ===

### Categories - Get all
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories

### Categories - Create (the response id is reused by the product requests below)
# @name createCategory
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo category {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Created from the .http file"
}

### Categories - Get by id
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}

### Categories - Get products by category
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}/products

### Categories - Update
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated demo category {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Updated from the .http file"
}


### === PRODUCTS ===

### Products - list (paged)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Products?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10

### Products - filter by category
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Products?categoryId={{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}&pageNumber=1&pageSize=10

### Products - search by name
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Products?search=lap&pageNumber=1&pageSize=10

### Products - Create (stock 10; the stock requests below use this product)
# @name createProduct
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Laptop",
  "price": 999.99,
  "stock": 10,
  "createdAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
  "categoryId": {{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
}

### Products - Get by id
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### Products - Update
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Laptop Pro",
  "price": 1299.99,
  "stock": 10,
  "createdAt": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
  "categoryId": {{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
}


### === STOCK ADJUSTMENTS ===
### Run "Products - Create" above first. The product starts with stock 10.

### Stock adjustment - success (expect 200 and newStock = 9 the first time)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": -1,
  "reason": "Sold in store"
}

### Stock adjustment - restock (expect 200)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": 5,
  "reason": "Delivery received"
}

### Stock adjustment - more than available (expect 409 Conflict, stock unchanged)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": -1000,
  "reason": "Should be rejected"
}

### Stock adjustment - missing product (expect 404)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/99999999/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": -1,
  "reason": "No such product"
}

### Stock adjustment - out of range delta (expect 400)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": -5000,
  "reason": "Out of range"
}

### Stock adjustment - zero delta (expect 400)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": 0,
  "reason": "Does nothing"
}

### Stock adjustment - no token (expect 401)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}/stock-adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delta": -1,
  "reason": "Not logged in"
}


### === REPORTS ===

### Reports - Inventory value
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Reports/inventory-value

### Reports - Most expensive product
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Reports/most-expensive

### Reports - Out of stock products
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Reports/out-of-stock

### Reports - Category stats
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Reports/category-stats


### === CLEANUP (admin only) ===

### Products - Delete
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/Products/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: {{Token}}

### Categories - Delete
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/Categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: {{Token}}


### === REFRESH TOKEN FLOW ===

### 1. Login as the test user (register "testuser" above first).
### The refresh token is picked up automatically as {{savedRefreshToken}}.
# @name userLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "TestPassword123!"
}

### 2. Refresh, happy path. Expect 200 with a NEW access token and a new refresh token.
# @name refresh
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{savedRefreshToken}}"
}

### 3. Reuse detection: send the SAME (now rotated and revoked) token again.
### Run step 2 once, then run this. Expect 401.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{savedRefreshToken}}"
}

### 4. Garbage token, never issued. Expect 401.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "this-was-never-a-real-token-12345"
}

### 5. Empty token, caught by [Required] on RefreshRequestDto. Expect 400.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": ""
}


### === LOGOUT FLOW ===

### 6. Login again to get a fresh token pair (run "1. Login as the test user" again).

### 7. Logout: needs a valid ACCESS token (admin login above works) and the refresh token to revoke.
### Expect 204 No Content.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/logout
Authorization: {{Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{savedRefreshToken}}"
}

### 8. Refresh with the token you just logged out with. Expect 401 (it is revoked).
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{savedRefreshToken}}"
}